    &gd.image.description;

     file


&gd.image.path;



        &null; is invalid if the compressed arguments is
        not used.





     compressed



       Whether the BMP should be compressed with run-length encoding (RLE), or not.


       Only BMPs with 4 or 8 bits per pixel can be compressed; for other bit
       depths, this parameter is ignored.

&reftitle.changelog;





    &Version;
    &Description;





    8.6.0

     The bundled GD library now saves truecolor images that are not fully
     opaque with 32 bits per pixel, and palette images with 1, 4, or 8 bits
     per pixel, depending on the number of colors in their palette.
     Previously, truecolor images were always saved with 24 bits per pixel,
     and palette images with 8 bits per pixel.


   &gd.changelog.image-param;


    8.0.0

     The type of compressed is &boolean; now; formerly it was &integer;.

  &reftitle.examples;



    Saving a BMP file


<?php
// Create a blank image and add some text
$im = imagecreatetruecolor(120, 20);
$text_color = imagecolorallocate($im, 233, 14, 91);

imagestring($im, 1, 5, 5,  'BMP with PHP', $text_color);

// Save the image
imagebmp($im, 'php.bmp');
?>





   Saving a 1-bit BMP

    As of PHP 8.6.0, with the bundled GD library, an image converted to a
    palette with 2 colors is saved with 1 bit per pixel, as expected by
    devices such as thermal printers.



<?php
$im = imagecreatetruecolor(120, 40);
imagefill($im, 0, 0, imagecolorallocate($im, 255, 255, 255));
imagestring($im, 5, 10, 12, 'Total: 9.99', imagecolorallocate($im, 0, 0, 0));

// Reduce the image to 2 colors, using dithering
imagetruecolortopalette($im, true, 2);

imagebmp($im, 'receipt.bmp');
?>
